.SS "License options"
Show the active license, install one, or renew it. With no argument it reports
what license this machine is using, where it came from, and when it expires.
With a file argument (or \- to read stdin) it validates the license and
installs it to the config directory, backing up any license already there.
With renew it asks the license service for a fresh license for the current
subscription, verifies the reply against the signing keys built into this
binary BEFORE writing a single byte, and installs it; a reply that does not
verify is discarded and nothing is written. Verification is not
signature\-only: the reply must carry the same license id and move the expiry
forward, so a valid artifact belonging to another subscription is refused too.
Renewal happens only when you type it \- check, the recall verbs, serve, and
guard never renew on their own \- and it is the only network call skarn makes
besides the opt\-in maintained\-feed fetch. The endpoint defaults to
https://api.getskarn.com and is overridable with $SKARN_LICENSE_RENEW_URL; it
must be https (plain http is accepted only against loopback), so a poisoned
environment cannot send the license anywhere in cleartext. Renew exits 0 when
the new license is installed, 1 when the service cannot be reached, 2 when the
service declines (its reason is printed verbatim), and 3 when the reply fails
verification. It never prints the license token itself, and it works without a
license \- and with an expired one \- so it never exits 5.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIpath\fR
Write the renewed license to this path instead of the config directory. Only
applies to `skarn license renew`; the file is written with owner\-only
permissions, and an existing file that is not a readable Skarn license is
never overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Replace an already\-installed license without asking. Required when installing
over an existing license from a script or from stdin, where there is no
terminal to confirm on.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the license status as a single JSON object (state, tier, licensee, org,
seats, license id, issue and expiry dates, days remaining, and the source it
was resolved from). The license token is never included.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
Clean, or informational output only.
.TP
\fB1\fR
A finding at or above the \-\-fail\-on\-severity threshold was reported. For
setup and guard \-\-self\-test: a target was refused or a verification failed.
For doctor: at least one check FAILED (a warning never exits nonzero, and
\-\-json always exits 0). Also: the first\-run EULA prompt was declined, so
the invoked operation was not performed.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The session risk score exceeded the \-\-fail\-on\-risk threshold. For setup:
no terminal to prompt on and no \-\-yes; the exact non\-interactive command is
printed.
.TP
\fB3\fR
A canary token was triggered (a proven breach). This overrides every other
gate.
.TP
\fB4\fR
A policy precondition was not met: a required rule is missing, or the policy
requires a baseline and none was supplied.
.TP
\fB5\fR
A requested paid feature is not covered by the active license (a Team or
Enterprise flag without a matching license). Refused before any scan. With no
usable license at all, check exits 7 before this gate is consulted.
.TP
\fB6\fR
The scan could not complete: session discovery or the scan itself failed. For
vet: the home directory could not be resolved (so the configuration was never
located at all), or a config file that exists could not be read, so the
configuration was only partly seen. Fail\-closed \- the result is not
trustworthy, so it is never reported as clean.
.TP
\fB7\fR
No usable license is present \- none was found via SKARN_LICENSE,
SKARN_LICENSE_FILE, or the installed file \- so check refused before scanning.
The free license is issued at https://getskarn.com/free after a quick email
confirmation and is verified offline. Also used when a license IS present but
cannot be used at all (revoked, tampered, or signed by an untrusted key).
assess, the recall commands, guard, setup, doctor, vet, license, taxonomies
and check \-\-audit\-verify never exit 7.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBSKARN_SCAN_THREADS\fR
Cap the worker\-pool size for every parallel sweep (scan and recall). 1 forces
a fully serial run. Default is one worker per core, capped at 32. Output is
identical for any value; only latency changes.
.TP
\fBSKARN_CLAUDE_DIRS\fR
Colon\-separated list of additional Claude Code config directories to scan
beyond the default ~/.claude. Each entry is the dir that contains projects/.
Roots are de\-duplicated.
.TP
\fBSKARN_TZ_OFFSET\fR
Default timezone offset in hours applied when grouping recall and stats output
by time.
.TP
\fBSKARN_NO_TIMING\fR
Suppress the dim "Scanned N sessions" timing line that recall commands print
after a text run on a terminal. Already auto\-suppressed for json/sarif/csv
output and for non\-TTY stdout.
.TP
\fBSKARN_LICENSE_RENEW_URL\fR
License\-service endpoint `skarn license renew` posts to. Defaults to
https://api.getskarn.com/v1/license/renew; set it to route renewals through an
enterprise proxy. It must be https \- plain http is accepted only against
loopback \- so a poisoned environment cannot redirect the license token to a
cleartext endpoint. No other command reads it.
.TP
\fBSKARN_GUARD_LOG\fR
Path to append a redacted JSONL verdict log for guard (opt\-in; off when
unset). One record per flagged call, carrying the fingerprint that `skarn
guard accept` takes; clean calls, and calls whose every finding was already
accepted, are not logged.
.TP
\fBSKARN_IDENTITY\fR
Local\-first identity tag (an SSO subject, email, or CI principal) stamped as
provenance on baseline entries created with \-\-baseline\-create. Optional;
Skarn never authenticates it.
.TP
\fBSKARN_ORG\fR
Local\-first org or team tag stamped alongside SKARN_IDENTITY on baseline
provenance. Optional.
.TP
\fBSKARN_FEED_URL\fR
Default feed channel URL used by check \-\-update\-rules when \-\-feed\-url is
not given (Team).
.TP
\fBSKARN_FEED_TOKEN\fR
Credential presented to the subscriber feed channel when fetching a maintained
feed (Team).
.TP
\fBSKARN_EULA_ACCEPTED\fR
Set to 1 to suppress the first\-run EULA prompt and notice for this run
without recording anything (ephemeral environments: containers, CI). Running
Skarn constitutes acceptance either way; `skarn eula accept` records it
durably instead.
.TP
\fBSKARN_LICENSE\fR
License token, resolved before SKARN_LICENSE_FILE and the config path.
.TP
\fBSKARN_LICENSE_FILE\fR
Path to a file containing a license token.
.TP
\fBCLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\fR
A Claude Code config directory visible in Skarn's environment; folded into the
claude source like an SKARN_CLAUDE_DIRS entry.
.TP
\fBCOPILOT_HOME\fR
GitHub Copilot CLI config directory visible in Skarn's environment; replaces
the default ~/.copilot as the Copilot CLI session root, folded into the
copilot source.
.TP
\fBCODEX_HOME\fR
A Codex CLI data directory visible in Skarn's environment; folded into the
codex source alongside the default ~/.codex, de\-duplicated, resolved via
expandPath. Each root contributes its sessions/ and archived_sessions/
children.
.TP
\fBSKARN_MANAGED_ROOT\fR
Prefix doctor prepends to every managed (MDM/fleet) config path it reads, so a
fleet admin can validate a staged payload directory before pushing it to a
single machine (SKARN_MANAGED_ROOT=/tmp/stage skarn doctor). Empty or unset
means the live system paths. Whenever it is active, doctor echoes the root in
the report header and emits it as managed_root in \-\-json, so a staged report
can never pass as a report about the live machine. Only doctor reads it.
.TP
\fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR
Base directory for the rule and feed cache. Defaults to ~/.cache, so the cache
lives in ~/.cache/skarn/.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed\-settings.json, /etc/claude\-code/managed\-settings.json, C:\eProgram Files\eClaudeCode\emanaged\-settings.json\fR
Claude Code's MDM\-managed settings (macOS, Linux/WSL, Windows). Doctor reads
the platform's path as the claude host's managed precedence layer;
allowManagedHooksOnly: true there makes every lower layer inert. Read\-only;
never written.
.TP
\fB/Library/Managed Preferences/com.anthropic.claudecode.plist\fR
Claude Code's macOS managed\-preferences domain. Declared as a managed source
but not decoded; when present, doctor surfaces it as a coverage gap with a
plutil command to inspect it, never as a silent absent.
.TP
\fB/etc/codex/requirements.toml, %ProgramData%\eOpenAI\eCodex\erequirements.toml\fR
Codex's admin\-managed requirements file (Unix, Windows). Doctor reads it as
the codex host's managed precedence layer via a scoped reader
(allow_managed_hooks_only and the [[hooks.<Event>.hooks]] command strings);
allow_managed_hooks_only = true makes every lower layer inert. Read\-only;
never written.
.TP
\fB/Library/Managed Preferences/com.openai.codex.plist\fR
Codex's macOS managed\-preferences domain. Doctor decodes the XML form
(requirements_toml_base64 and config_toml_base64, base64 to the same scoped
reader; the lockdown key is honored only from the requirements payload,
matching Codex); a binary plist is surfaced as present\-but\-unreadable with
the exact plutil conversion command, never as a silent absent.
.TP
\fB/Library/Application Support/Cursor/hooks.json, /etc/cursor/hooks.json, C:\eProgramData\eCursor\ehooks.json\fR
Cursor's enterprise\-managed hooks (macOS, Linux/WSL, Windows). Doctor reads
the platform's path as the cursor host's managed precedence layer; Cursor
layers additively (no lockdown key), so every present layer stays active.
Read\-only; never written.
.TP
\fB/etc/github\-copilot/policy.d/*.json, C:\eProgramData\eGitHub\eCopilot\epolicy.d\e*.json\fR
Copilot's managed policy directory (Linux/macOS, Windows). Doctor folds every
*.json in the directory into the copilot host's managed precedence layer,
sorted by name; Copilot layers additively. Read\-only; never written.
.TP
\fB./.claude/settings.local.json\fR
Claude Code's personal, gitignored project settings file. Claude merges hooks
across every settings file and runs all of them, so a guard wired here
protects this checkout and doctor reads it as part of the project layer. skarn
setup never writes it: it writes only the committed ./.claude/settings.json.
.TP
\fB./.claude/settings.json, ./.cursor/hooks.json, ./.codex/hooks.json, ./.github/hooks/skarn.json\fR
A repo's committed project\-scope hook configs (claude, cursor, codex,
copilot), written by skarn setup \-\-scope project and read by doctor as each
host's project precedence layer whenever it runs in that directory. Portable
by construction: the committed command resolves skarn from PATH at run time
and exits 0 where skarn is not installed.
.TP
\fB~/.skarn.json\fR
Optional tool configuration: the set of assistant tools and their session
paths, plus an optional projects alias map. Both the recall surface and scan
discovery (check, assess, baseline audit, the guard's stop advisory, and
serve's Security scan) read it, so the security scan and the recall views
cover the same corpus. Falls back to a builtin tool set when absent. The
projects object renames a resolved project for display: a key beginning ~, $,
or / is a path prefix (with ~ and a leading $VAR expanded like sessions_path)
matched against the canonical project root on whole path components, longest
match winning (so /repo never matches /repository); any other key matches the
derived display name case\-insensitively; the value is the shown name. Aliases
change display only, never the grouping key.
.TP
\fB~/.cache/skarn/\fR
Cache for downloaded rule and maintained\-feed bundles. Honors
$XDG_CACHE_HOME.
.TP
\fB~/.config/skarn/baseline.json\fR
The personal accepted\-findings baseline, applied automatically when it
exists: check, assess, and serve suppress its findings, and guard stops
flagging them. Written by `skarn baseline audit/accept` and `skarn guard
accept`. Honors $XDG_CONFIG_HOME. Holds fingerprints and hashes, never a raw
secret; treat it as sensitive.
.TP
\fB~/.config/skarn/eula\-accepted.json\fR
The EULA acceptance record: the agreement version accepted, an RFC\-3339
timestamp, and the method (prompt, command, env, license\-install). Written
when acceptance is given at the first\-run prompt, by `skarn eula accept`, or
by installing a License Token; never transmitted. Honors $XDG_CONFIG_HOME.
.TP
\fB~/.claude/\fR
Default Claude Code session root. Scanned automatically; extend with
$SKARN_CLAUDE_DIRS or $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR.
.TP
\fB~/.claude/settings.json, ~/.claude/settings.local.json\fR
Claude Code hooks and permission grants. Read (never written) by vet, and by
the project\-local ./.claude/settings.json and ./.claude/settings.local.json
when one exists.
.TP
\fB~/.claude.json, ~/.mcp.json\fR
Claude Code MCP server definitions. Read by vet, along with a project\-local
\&./.mcp.json when one exists.
.TP
\fB~/.claude/plugins/, ~/.claude/skills/\fR
Installed Claude Code plugins and skills. Vet reads each plugin.json and
skill.json manifest for its install source and integrity marker.
.TP
\fB~/.codex/sessions/, ~/.codex/archived_sessions/\fR
Default Codex CLI session roots, scanned automatically and extendable with
$CODEX_HOME. zstd\-compressed rollouts (rollout\-*.jsonl.zst, written for
rollouts older than 7 days) are read transparently through the same reader as
plain ones; when both a plain rollout and its .zst twin exist the plain one is
preferred. Only rollout\-* files are parsed as sessions, so
session_index.jsonl is never scanned.
.TP
\fB~/.codex/config.toml, ~/.codex/hooks.json\fR
Codex CLI MCP server definitions and hooks. Read by vet.
.TP
\fB~/.cursor/mcp.json, ~/.cursor/hooks.json\fR
Cursor MCP server definitions and hooks. Read by vet.
.TP
\fB~/.copilot/mcp\-config.json, ~/.copilot/config.json\fR
Copilot CLI MCP server definitions and configuration. Read by vet.
.TP
\fB~/.gemini/settings.json\fR
Gemini CLI MCP server definitions. Read by vet.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show which license this machine is using, where it came from, and when it
expires.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn license
.EE
.RE
.PP
Validate a license file and install it; the previous license, if any, is
backed up alongside it.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn license ~/Downloads/team.skarnlicense
.EE
.RE
.PP
Fetch a fresh license for this subscription, verify it against the keys built
into this binary, and install it; nothing is written unless it verifies.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn license renew
.EE
.RE
.PP
Scan every AI coding session on this machine and print a friendly risk summary
in one command; no flags, no license.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn assess
.EE
.RE
.PP
Write a self\-contained, redacted security report to share with a colleague;
\-o report.md writes a plain\-text version.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn assess \-o report.html
.EE
.RE
.PP
Statically vet this machine's AI assistant configuration \- hooks, MCP
servers, permission grants, plugins and skills \- and list the risky patterns
found. Read\-only, offline, no license.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn vet
.EE
.RE
.PP
Emit the config findings as SARIF for a code\-scanning pipeline and exit 1 on
anything high or above; an unreadable config file exits 6 rather than
reporting a partial view as clean.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn vet \-\-format sarif \-\-fail\-on\-severity high
.EE
.RE
.PP
Detect installed AI coding agents and wire the guard hook into each one in
audit mode, with a wizard on a terminal; ends with the guard self\-test and a
list of every file touched.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn setup
.EE
.RE
.PP
Print the exact Cursor hooks.json content that setup would write, without
writing anything.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn setup \-\-print \-\-agent cursor
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check that skarn is really protecting this machine: license, every wired agent
hook, the guard log, and the guard self\-test. Each warning or failure names
the command that fixes it.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn doctor
.EE
.RE
.PP
The same checks as one JSON object for fleet scripts; the check ids are stable
and always exits 0.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn doctor \-\-json
.EE
.RE
.PP
Flip every agent that already carries skarn entries from audit to enforce,
leaving everything else alone.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn setup \-\-update \-\-mode enforce
.EE
.RE
.PP
Summarize the last 30 days of flagged calls per agent (verdicts, top rules,
latency, the most recent denies) and, when the window is clean, print the
exact command that flips the hooks to enforce.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn guard report \-\-window 30d
.EE
.RE
.PP
The same aggregate as one JSON object for fleet scripts: counts are over
flagged actions, since the guard does not log clean calls.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn guard report \-\-format json
.EE
.RE
.PP
Accept a finding the guard flagged (the fingerprint printed under the deny in
guard report) as a false positive, so the identical call stops being blocked.
Writes the personal baseline the guard reads; a real leak is never accepted
this way.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn guard accept 7d343e3a105ae026589b3371d565a4ad2943dd5ba5f81a19c7500b2ab4dbb1f0 \-\-reason 'internal test credential'
.EE
.RE
.PP
Prove the guard wiring: run synthetic benign and fake\-credential events
through each adapter's real code path and report the verdicts (credential
shown redacted).
.RS 4
.EX
skarn guard \-\-self\-test
.EE
.RE
.PP
Scan the default window (the last 30 days) of all sessions for leaked secrets
and attack patterns.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn check
.EE
.RE
.PP
Scan all history, report only high\-severity\-and\-above findings, and emit
JSON for a pipeline.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn check \-\-hours 0 \-\-severity high \-\-format json
.EE
.RE
.PP
Exit non\-zero in CI when a session's risk score exceeds 60.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn check \-\-fail\-on\-risk 60
.EE
.RE
.PP
Search past sessions for a regular\-expression pattern.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn search 'AWS_SECRET' \-\-regex
.EE
.RE
.PP
List recent Claude Code sessions.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn recent \-\-cli claude
.EE
.RE
.PP
Render per\-project analytics to a self\-contained HTML file.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn stats \-\-by project \-\-format html \-o stats.html
.EE
.RE
.PP
Browse and scan sessions in a local web UI on 127.0.0.1:7777 (localhost only,
no egress); open the token\-carrying URL printed at startup.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn serve \-\-port 7777
.EE
.RE
.PP
Serve the web UI with a custom rule pack layered on the bundled rules; the
Security view surfaces its findings too.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn serve \-\-rules ./team\-rules.toml
.EE
.RE
.PP
Walk each new finding and label it a true or false positive with a reason; the
decisions are written into the committed baseline and survive re\-scans.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn baseline audit .skarn\-baseline.json
.EE
.RE
.PP
Record a single false\-positive fingerprint (from SARIF partialFingerprints or
the ndjson skarn.fingerprint field) into the baseline without the interactive
loop.
.RS 4
.EX
skarn baseline accept .skarn\-baseline.json 7d343e3a105ae026589b3371d565a4ad2943dd5ba5f81a19c7500b2ab4dbb1f0 \-\-reason 'internal test credential'
.EE
.RE
.SH SECURITY
Skarn scans locally and makes no network connection by default. Secrets are
redacted in every output format unless \-\-no\-redact is given.
.PP
The only feature that transmits anything off the machine is the maintained
feed: \-\-update\-rules and \-\-feed\-url fetch a signed feed bundle from the
subscriber channel. No secret ever leaves the machine. It is off by default
and is disabled by \-\-offline.
.PP
skarn vet reads the AI assistant configuration files listed under FILES
read\-only: it opens each one for reading, never writes, rewrites, or removes
one, and makes no network call. It reports what it finds and leaves every
decision about the configuration to you. \-\-offline is accepted for parity
and changes nothing.
